der_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Movado Group, Inc. designs, sources, markets, and distributes watches worldwide. It operates in two segments, Watch and Accessory Brands, and Company Stores. The company offers its watches under the Movado, Concord, Ebel, Olivia Burton, and MVMT brands, as well as licensed brands comprising Coach, Tommy Hilfiger, HUGO BOSS, Lacoste, Calvin Klein, and KATE SPADE NEW YORK. It also designs, sources, markets, and distributes jewelry and other accessories; and provides after-sales and shipping services. The company's customers include jewelry store chains, department stores, independent regional jewelers, network of independent distributors, online marketplaces, licensors' retail stores, and third-party e-commerce retailers. It sells directly to consumers through its e-commerce platforms. The company was formerly known as North American Watch Corporation and changed its name to Movado Group, Inc. in 1996. Movado Group, Inc. was founded in 1881 and is headquartered in Paramus, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Efraim  Grinberg | Chairman & CEO | Age 67 | Compensation: $3.3M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 991 people. Revenue per employee of $677K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $54K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Movado Group Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $709M market cap on $671M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 9% cost of capital, a 7-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it. Gross margins of 54% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $53M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 59\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 4.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 4.2% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 16% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 34% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(MOV) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/34/MOV_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_110926075202_1794228722.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794228722.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (MOV) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/21/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_MOV_Movement_103026084002_1793364002.html","date":"2026-10-30","timestamp":1793364002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"3 US Retail Importer Stocks That Could Gain From Tariff Refunds","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/3-us-retail-importer-stocks-171204773.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794503524.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.784,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["regulatory"]},{"title":"Texas Roadhouse (TXRH) Misses Q3 Earnings and Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024935/texas-roadhouse-txrh-misses-q3-earnings-and-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3024935","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793915103.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.226,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]}