r-to-year swings of 29%).","At current returns, reinvesting 96% of profits supports about 16.2% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -4.0% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex runs only 0.5x depreciation (0.7% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is 13, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 96.6% on average."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.2%, and institutions hold 99%.","It returns 4.9% a year to shareholders (0.6% in buybacks and 5.0% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 0.9% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 991 employees, each generates about $677K of revenue, 1.8x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 2.4% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $54K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $3.3M (5x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $5K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INVEST","conv":87,"head":"Invest: trades 34% below fair value of $48.07; ROIC 16.9% vs WACC 9.5%.","pros":["Composite 44, above the 39 line (gates 13/24)","Trades 34% below fair value of $48.07","ROIC 16.9% vs WACC 9.5%","Net cash of $230.5M","Piotroski F-score 7/9"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":40.86,"vc":{"base":48.07,"base_src":"dcf","bear":38.13,"bull":62.04,"alt_median":27.11,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.1508,"dispersion":0.3879,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (39% dispersion)","DCF is 115% above the other models' median ($27.11)"]},"med":{"pe":18.8184,"ev_ebitda":10.707,"pfcf":16.6971,"pb":2.3,"roic":0.1268,"gross_margin":0.346,"fcf_margin":0.0621,"div_yield":0.0232}},"mc_quantiles":[32.04,36.28,38.13,40.16,41.3,42.58,43.8,44.91,46.09,47.22,48.21,49.33,50.64,51.94,53.52,54.89,56.74,58.9,62.04,66.26,75.9],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.704,"discount_rate":0.259,"terminal_growth":0.021,"exit_multiple"